---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Terms of Use | BabelDoc';
const description =
  'Read the terms for BabelDoc’s free online tools. Tools are provided as-is and are not professional advice. You keep what you create. Review the terms first.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} ogTitle="BabelDoc terms of use">
  <article class="max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl leading-tight text-ink">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">Effective date: November 19, 2026</p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7">
      These terms cover your use of BabelDoc at getbabeldoc.com. If you do not agree with them, do not use the site.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink">Using the tools</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7">
        The tools are free and provided as they are. They are a convenience for everyday tasks. A count, conversion, or generated result is not professional, legal, medical, financial, or academic advice, and it is not a guarantee that a third party will accept the result.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7">
        You are responsible for checking a result before you rely on it. The word counter documents its own counting rules on that page. Other tools will do the same.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink">Acceptable use</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7">Do not use the site to break the law, to attack the site or other people, or to scrape it so heavily that it interferes with normal use. Do not try to bypass access limits or probe the site for vulnerabilities without permission.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink">Intellectual property</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7">
        The BabelDoc name, the text on these pages, and the site’s code belong to the site. You may not copy the site and present it as your own.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7">
        Text or other material you put into a tool stays yours. BabelDoc does not claim ownership of it. You are responsible for having the right to use that material.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink">Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7">
        The site is provided without warranties of any kind, including fitness for a particular purpose and uninterrupted availability. To the extent the law allows, BabelDoc is not liable for lost data, lost time, or decisions you make from a tool’s result.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink">Governing law</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7">
        No governing law is named here yet. The operator has not designated a jurisdiction. This section will be updated when that choice is made. Until then, these terms still describe how the tools may be used.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink">Contact</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7">
        Questions about these terms can go to <a class="text-accent underline-offset-4 hover:underline" href="mailto:hello@getbabeldoc.com">hello@getbabeldoc.com</a>.
        See also the <a class="text-accent underline-offset-4 hover:underline" href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>
        and the <a class="text-accent underline-offset-4 hover:underline" href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
